If he runs X11 on his mac and uses ssh with X11 forwarding enabled, he
should be able to get the graphics.  I've never played any other way
than ASCII terminal mode, but as I understand it, the QT interface is
just runs nethach as an X11 application with widgets/tilesets/etc.

The easiest way I know of is to use ssh with a config file that looks
like this:

Host [name]
HostName [name2]
User [username]
ForwardX11 yes

Where [name] is the name your roommate would use in the 'ssh [name]'
command.  [name2] is the computer's name on the local network (or a
FQDN for an external machine).  [name] and [name2] may well be the
same on a LAN.  [username] should be obvious, and the last option is
the one that does the magic of exporting X11 apps from the server and
displaying them on the client.

